ALGORITHM A* search

Start with node S.
Set g(S) = 0.
Calculate f(n) = g(n) + h(n).
Put S into OPEN list.
Repeat until OPEN is empty:
      a. Select the node with the lowest f value.
      b. Remove it from OPEN.
      c. If the node is G:
            Return the path and cost.
      d. Expand all neighbouring nodes.
      e. Calculate:
            g(child) = g(current) + edge cost
            f(child) = g(child) + h(child)
      f. Add/update the child in OPEN.
If OPEN becomes empty, return "No path".
Stop.
